# Example crontabs of the BARF Nutri server (docs/13-nasazeni-a-provoz.md, §13.7 and §13.8).
# The file holds TWO crontabs, one per operating-system account; install each one with
# "crontab -u ACCOUNT FILE" (or crontab -e as that account) and adjust the paths:
#
#   barf-backup  backup and restore test. It owns the backup directory, the encryption
#                passphrase and the pgpass file; the account of the web application cannot
#                read or write any of them (an attacker who gets code execution in the web
#                process then cannot read, decrypt or delete the backups).
#   barf         the account of the application: the daily Django jobs only.
#
# /opt/barf and /opt/barf/deploy belong to root and are not writable by either account.
# Nothing secret belongs in this file: the scripts read their configuration from the files
# below (mode 600), and cron mails the output of a job only when the job fails.
#
#   /etc/barf/ops.env      owner barf-backup. POSTGRES_* of a read-only backup role, BACKUP_DIR,
#                          BACKUP_PASSPHRASE_FILE (read by backup_db.sh through BARF_ENV_FILE)
#   /etc/barf/restore.env  owner barf-backup. The same, but POSTGRES_USER is a role with
#                          CREATEDB, plus RESTORE_TEST_LOG (read by restore_test.sh)
#   /etc/barf/app.env      owner barf. The variables of .env.example (read by run_manage.sh)
#
# app.env is PARSED by run_manage.sh, never run by a shell: NAME=value lines, a value may be
# wrapped in one pair of quotes (DJANGO_DEFAULT_FROM_EMAIL='BARF Nutri <noreply@barf.example.cz>'),
# nothing is expanded. A generated DJANGO_SECRET_KEY can be written as it is.
#
# The hours below are in the time zone set by CRON_TZ (cron implementations without CRON_TZ use
# the server time zone). Backup file names and the protocol of the restore test are always UTC.

# ===== crontab of the account barf-backup ======================================================

SHELL=/bin/bash
CRON_TZ=Europe/Prague
MAILTO=admin@barf.example.cz
BARF_ENV_FILE=/etc/barf/ops.env

# minute hour day-of-month month day-of-week  command

# Daily encrypted backup, then retention: the newest 30 backups and the first backup of each of
# the last 12 months are kept. Failure (non-zero exit) is mailed to MAILTO.
17 2 * * * /opt/barf/deploy/backup_db.sh >>/var/log/barf-backup/backup.log 2>&1 || echo "BARF backup FAILED, see /var/log/barf-backup/backup.log"

# Monthly restore test of the newest backup into a scratch database (docs/07 §7.7). Runs on the
# 3rd of the month, after the backup of that night; appends one line to RESTORE_TEST_LOG.
# The database role needs CREATEDB. FAIL (non-zero exit) is mailed to MAILTO.
41 4 3 * * BARF_ENV_FILE=/etc/barf/restore.env /opt/barf/deploy/restore_test.sh >>/var/log/barf-backup/restore-test.log 2>&1 || echo "BARF restore test FAILED, see /var/log/barf-backup/restore-test.log"

# ===== crontab of the account barf (the application) ===========================================

SHELL=/bin/bash
CRON_TZ=Europe/Prague
MAILTO=admin@barf.example.cz
APP_ENV_FILE=/etc/barf/app.env

# Daily: delete registrations nobody activated within 7 days (PENDING_ACCOUNT_RETENTION).
23 3 * * * /opt/barf/deploy/run_manage.sh purge_pending_accounts >>/var/log/barf/jobs.log 2>&1 || echo "BARF purge_pending_accounts FAILED, see /var/log/barf/jobs.log"

# Daily: delete expired sessions from the database.
29 3 * * * /opt/barf/deploy/run_manage.sh clearsessions >>/var/log/barf/jobs.log 2>&1 || echo "BARF clearsessions FAILED, see /var/log/barf/jobs.log"
